      "pronunciations": [
        "/tʃeɪndʒ/"
      ],
      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "当前语境",
          "lines": [
            "折叠摘要：文中为趋势主题：本句 与 本句，这里强调其在当前表达中的具体含义和作用。",
            "展开解析：文中为趋势主题：\"...the changing trends in the average number...\" 与 \"The most striking change is seen in...\"",
            "**考研英语一 2011 Text 1 补充**：If Gilbert and the Philharmonic are to succeed, they must first change the relationship between America's oldest orchestra and the new audience it hopes to attract."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "词源与构词",
          "lines": [
            "词源/构词: 源自古法语 changier，再溯至拉丁语 cambiare\"交换\"。",
            "原始画面: 同一事物前后不同，或一手交一手的交换。",
            "核心意象: 前后不同 + 交换 = change。"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "用法边界",
          "lines": [
            "典型搭配: change trend；bring about change；climate change",
            "近义词区别: change 最通用；shift 强调方向性转移；transformation 强调根本性蜕变。",
            "常见误用: \"变化趋势\"是 changing trends（现在分词作定语），不是 changed trends。"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "深层解释",
          "lines": [
            "change / changing trends 是图表作文第一段描述数据变动的核心词，与 rise、increase、surge 形成语义梯度。"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "一语道破",
          "lines": [
            "\"Change is the same thing wearing a different face. 变化，是同一事物换了一副面孔。\""
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "来源信息",
          "lines": [
            "来源段落：2011 English I Cloze: Laughter and Emotion，第 1 段"
          ]
        },
        {
