      "pronunciations": [
        "/ˌkɒrɪˈspɒnd tuː/"
      ],
      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "当前语境",
          "lines": [
            "考研英语一 2012 Text 3：...a process that corresponds to what philosopher Annette Baier has described as the commons of the mind."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "词源与构词",
          "lines": [
            "- **词源/构词**: correspond 来自拉丁语 correspondere，cor-（共同）+ respondere（回应），即“相互回应”。",
            "- **原始画面**: 两把钥匙分别对应两个锁孔，刚好匹配。",
            "- **核心意象**: 相互 + 回应 + 匹配 = correspond to"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "用法边界",
          "lines": [
            "- **典型搭配**: correspond to reality；correspond to description；correspond with sb",
            "- **近义词区别**: match 强调完全匹配；correspond to 强调“相互对应、一致”，常用于抽象关系。",
            "- **常见误用**: correspond with 可指“与……通信”，correspond to 多指“与……对应/一致”。"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "深层解释",
          "lines": [
            "Correspond to 在本文中把 credibility process 与 commons of the mind 两个抽象概念连接起来，说明前者是后者在科学领域的具体体现。它强调结构上的对应关系，而非简单相似。",
            "The results correspond to our predictions. 结果与预测相符。"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "一语道破",
          "lines": [
            "\"To correspond is to answer each other across difference. 对应，是跨越差异后的相互回应。\""
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "note": "考研英语一 2012 Text 3"
      }
    },
    {
      "word": "Conception",
      "definition": "概念；理解；构想",
      "fileName": "4930-conception.md",
      "lookupKey": "conception",
      "partOfSpeech": "名词",
      "pronunciations": [
        "/kənˈsepʃn/"
      ],
      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "当前语境",
          "lines": [
            "考研英语一 2012 Text 3：\"We reason together, challenge, revise, and complete each other's reasoning and each other's conceptions of reason.\"",
            "考研英语一 2013 Text 1：This top-down conception of the fashion business couldn't be more out of date."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "词源与构词",
          "lines": [
            "- **词源/构词**: 来自拉丁语 conceptio，capere（抓住、理解），即“心中抓住一个想法”。",
            "- **原始画面**: 头脑中形成一个清晰的形状，像雕塑家捏出雏形。",
            "- **核心意象**: 抓住 + 观念 + 理解 = conception"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "用法边界",
          "lines": [
            "- **典型搭配**: conception of reason；have a conception of；conception of justice；my conception of happiness",
            "- **近义词区别**: concept 指抽象概念；conception 强调“个人对某事物的理解/构想”，带主观性。",
            "- **常见误用**: 不要与 perception（感知）混淆；conception 更强调理性构建。"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "深层解释",
          "lines": [
            "Conception of reason 指“对理性的理解”。本文强调科学共同体不仅共同推理，还共同修正彼此对“理性”本身的理解。这比一般 concept 更深层。",
            "Different cultures have different conceptions of time. 不同文化对时间有不同理解。"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "一语道破",
          "lines": [
            "\"Conception is the mind's grasp of what reason means. 概念，是心智对理性含义的把握。\""
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "note": "考研英语一 2012 Text 3"
      }
    },
    {
      "word": "Intellectual credit",
      "definition": "学术荣誉；智力贡献的认可",
      "fileName": "4931-intellectual-credit.md",
      "lookupKey": "intellectual-credit",
      "partOfSpeech": "名词短语",
      "pronunciations": [
        "/ˌɪntəˈlektʃuəl ˈkredɪt/"
      ],
      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "当前语境",
          "lines": [
            "考研英语一 2012 Text 3：Once a discovery claim becomes public, the discoverer receives intellectual credit."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "词源与构词",
          "lines": [
            "- **词源/构词**: intellectual 来自拉丁语 intellectualis（理解的）；credit 来自 credere（相信），引申为“荣誉、认可”。",
            "- **原始画面**: 一块写着“学术贡献”的勋章，颁发给提出新思想的人。",
            "- **核心意象**: 智力 + 贡献 + 获得认可 = intellectual credit"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "用法边界",
          "lines": [
            "- **典型搭配**: receive intellectual credit；give credit to；intellectual credit for sth；credit for the discovery",
            "- **近义词区别**: honor 泛指荣誉；intellectual credit 特指学术/智力层面的认可。",
            "- **常见误用**: credit 在此不是“信用”或“学分”，而是“认可、荣誉”。"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "深层解释",
          "lines": [
            "本文中 intellectual credit 是发现声明公开后给予发现者的即时回报，与后文“共同体接管后续验证”形成对照：发现者获得荣誉，但发现本身能否可信还需共同体决定。",
            "Give credit where credit is due. 该认可时就认可。"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "一语道破",
          "lines": [
            "\"Intellectual credit is the honor ideas earn when they go public. 学术荣誉，是思想公开时所赢得的尊重。\""
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "note": "考研英语一 2012 Text 3"
      }
    },
    {
      "word": "Work one's way through",
      "definition": "逐步通过；努力推进",
      "fileName": "4932-work-one's-way-through.md",
      "lookupKey": "work-one's-way-through",
      "partOfSpeech": "短语动词",
      "pronunciations": [
        "/wɜːk wʌnz weɪ θruː/"
      ],
      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "当前语境",
          "lines": [
            "考研英语一 2012 Text 3：As a discovery claim works its way through the community..."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "词源与构词",
          "lines": [
            "- **词源/构词**: work（努力）+ one's way（道路）+ through（穿过），即“努力穿过”。",
            "- **原始画面**: 一步一步穿过人群或复杂地形，不断向前挪动。",
            "- **核心意象**: 努力 + 路径 + 穿越 = work one's way through"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "用法边界",
          "lines": [
            "- **典型搭配**: work one's way through college；work one's way through difficulties；work one's way through a crowd",
            "- **近义词区别**: pass through 仅指经过；work one's way through 强调“努力、逐步、克服困难”。",
            "- **常见误用**: 不要省略所有格：work one's way，不是 work the way through。"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "深层解释",
          "lines": [
            "本文用此短语描述 discovery claim 在科学共同体中层层推进、接受审查的缓慢过程。它不是自动滑过，而是需要在各个环节努力争取。",
            "She worked her way through law school by waiting tables. 她靠端盘子读完法学院。"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "一语道破",
          "lines": [
            "\"To work one's way through is to advance by effort, not by shortcut. 逐步推进，是努力前行而非走捷径。\""
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "note": "考研英语一 2012 Text 3"
      }
    },
